# org-target: docs/10-19-design/10-architecture/10.23-native-aitia-backpressure-content-review.org::#source-change-history-reassessment
# render-layout: elk; theme: 0; pad: 24; timeout: 30
direction: down
native: "Actual Rust variants / Core Ops\nA64: M06 counter\nB64: M04 + M06 counters\nC64 / C128: repaired owner and permit cuts"
intake: "Existing native ASCENT exchange\n22 original + 24 new observations\nComplete snapshot + attested query + owner / generation\nSeven counters retained; no scope-filtered history"
complete: "Exact failure-list closure\nNo omissions, duplicates or relabeled diagnostics\nUnavailable history retains known failures\nA new counter invalidates old membership and cut\nFixed cross-intake discovery -> 90.80\nGlobal discovery remains pending"
packet: "Native Aitia reassessment packet\nPolicy + revision / scope + source + manifest + Cargo.lock bytes\nHistory cut + failure IDs + pointwise repair references"
context: "Classification / context receipt\nReuse only exact valid native request\nNo new institutional authority"
dispose: "Pointwise disposition content receipts\nSame case + payload + new repaired source\nC64 cannot close the old 128-byte failure\nClones / expiry / revocation keep the blocker"
gate: "Existing native Aitia stage gate\nVerified pass + unresolved counter -> blocked\nComplete capture + valid dispositions -> bounded admission\nCounters remain historical facts; no release authority"
late: "Late B counter\nOld closure cannot certify the expanded intake\nFresh capture and new disposition bindings required"
source: "Real source D or Cargo.lock changes after review\nOld native correspondence is no longer current\nNew revision and smaller scope do not validate new bytes"
open: "Remaining boundaries\nHost-selected intake is not global history\nSigned test-authority controls -> 90.80\nInstitutional approval remains pending\nNo atomic use authorization or performance claim"
native -> intake -> complete -> packet
packet -> context -> gate
packet -> dispose -> gate
intake -> late -> complete: "recapture"
gate -> source -> packet: "reassess"
gate -> open
